<title>FRANCE: Danone 9-month sales 63.2 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Danone 9-month sales 63.2 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					63,229    vs   60,201</p>
<p>Western Europe</p>
<p>     - dairy products			   16,895    vs   16,519</p>
<p>     - grocery products/pasta		 11,690    vs   11,806</p>
<p>     - biscuits				    9,186    vs    8,690</p>
<p>     - beer					  5,838    vs    5,941</p>
<p>     - mineral water			     5,453    vs    5,656</p>
<p>     - containers				  4,915    vs    4,951</p>
<p>    International				 11,140    vs    8,588</p>
<p>NOTE - Food group Danone gave its sales figures in a statement. It said sales were up five percent, with organic growth of two percent to 1,249 million francs. Third quarter business was hit by poor weather which cut into beer and mineral water sales. Currency conversion differences, due mainly to the lira's rise and changes in sales structure, added 151 million francs to sales. First-time integration of dairy product operations in eastern Europe, China and Argentina, biscuits in Greece and China, and beer in China added 1,628 million francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
